      "date": "1990-07-18",
      "kind": "permit appeal",
      "description": "The Board of Permit Appeals upheld the departments and granted the permit to erect a structure at 142 Acadia Street, on conditions including deleting the wet bar from the basement room, changing the door to the basement mechanical area to a door clearly for non-pedestrian use, lowering the parapet to comply with the original plans, and changing the north-facing bay window to comply with the originally approved plans.",
